id: pm-rust-ax0o
title: Stabilize the create lock-replacement fixture under parallel load
description: "During pm-rust-ufzy aggregate validation, the unchanged Linux create_never_removes_a_lock_replaced_by_another_owner test failed once with a missing-file error; an immediate isolated rerun passed. The fixture observes lock-file existence before replacing its owner text, which may race the initial token write. Preserve the lock-ownership assertions while making fixture readiness deterministic; investigate before attributing this observation to production lock handling."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: concurrency,rust,testing
created_at: "2026-10-05T08:51:24.281Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-15T00:40:15.663Z"
author: codex-sol
acceptance_criteria: Repeated full-suite and isolated runs under concurrent load pass with the same replacement-owner preservation assertions; Fixture readiness proves the initial owner token is fully written before replacement; Existing four-metric coverage and release gates remain enforced
parent: pm-rust-u4al
comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-05T08:54:08.145Z",codex-sol,"The exact isolated test command also passed through pm test --run --progress, and the subsequent complete just release-check passed all 183 tests with all four coverage metrics at 100 percent. No mutation or create test assertions were changed in the pagination implementation. The intermittent observation still needs deterministic fixture investigation."
  "2026-10-14T20:34:44.763Z",codex-agent,"Implementing the native parity batch against the locked 2026.10.14 oracle. Evidence will compare real disposable trackers, complete output envelopes and durable artifacts, with a behavioral revert proof and unchanged release gates."
  "2026-10-14T20:43:02.960Z",codex-agent,"Replaced existence polling and sleeps with a FIFO writer/reader rendezvous: recovery opens the FIFO only after the lock owner token is initialized and synced. The test validates the complete token before replacing owner bytes, then releases recovery and independently checks replacement preservation. Parallel repetitions and a deterministic negative control are pending."
  "2026-10-14T20:55:42.122Z",codex-agent,"Parallel acceptance completed: 50/50 runs of cargo test --locked --test create_contract -- --test-threads=8 passed, totaling 350 tests and 50 successful replacement-owner preservation checks. The fixture contains no sleeps and synchronizes on recovery opening the FIFO after the owner token is synced."
  "2026-10-14T21:03:08.858Z",codex-agent,"Final fixture acceptance: after factoring the FIFO synchronization into a helper and adding the controlled delayed-owner regression plus a comparison with the published lock primitive, all 50/50 final create-suite runs passed with eight test threads. Exact command: PM_RUST_REQUIRE_PUBLISHED_CLI=1 cargo test --locked --test create_contract -- --test-threads=8 with the locked oracle selected. Total: 400 tests, 50 native/oracle replacement-preservation comparisons and 50 delayed-owner readiness regressions."
  "2026-10-14T21:33:39.453Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: cargo test --locked --test create_contract replacement_fixture_waits_for_initialized_owner -- --exact --nocapture compiled and failed at runtime with exit 101. Behaviorally restoring the former existence polling in the fixture helper writes replacement bytes before a deliberately paused owner initializes its token; the controlled readiness regression fails deterministically. The regression test stayed in place, and all source bytes were restored after the check."
  "2026-10-14T22:40:43.436Z",codex-agent,"The item-linked pinned-oracle command passed through pm test --run --only-last --progress --fail-on-skipped --fail-on-empty-test-run --json: 8 tests passed, zero failures or skips. Test-result tracking is disabled by project policy, so this append-only comment records the observed receipt. The behavioral revert failure is recorded separately. Final parallel repetition: 50/50 complete create_contract runs passed with eight test threads, 400 tests in total, including 50 published-oracle replacement comparisons and 50 controlled delayed-owner checks. No sleeps participate in synchronization."
  "2026-10-15T00:40:14.817Z",codex-agent,"Final Linux acceptance: just release-check passed at unchanged pins and thresholds in an isolated Git identity environment. Both the ordinary and fresh branch-instrumented suites passed 317 tests across 17 targets, with zero failures or ignored tests. Coverage: 5646/5646 lines, 8630/8630 regions, 522/522 functions and 1194/1194 branches, all 100 percent. Formatting, deny-warnings Clippy, private-item rustdoc, identity audit, locked-oracle differential suites, cargo audit and changelog check passed. Cargo audit retains the inherited allowed RUSTSEC-2024-0449 unmaintained advisory. Per-item behavioral revert proof and linked-test receipts remain recorded separately. Releasing ownership for orchestrator verification; this item remains in progress and is not closed. The final synchronized create fixture passed 50/50 complete create_contract runs with eight threads: 400 tests, 50 oracle replacement comparisons and 50 controlled readiness checks."
